      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Duplication is a deliberate tool, not a mistake",
            "Only question: does the copied field change often enough to hurt?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Consistency Ladder",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "single-doc atomic",
              "transaction",
              "change stream",
              "nightly job"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Left is correct and free; right is stalest and cheapest",
            "Transactions: 60 s default, cache pressure from held snapshots",
            "Retry logic for `TransientTransactionError` is mandatory"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking A Rung",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Single-document update: atomic, free, always first choice",
            "Change stream: eventual, cheap, resumable after a crash",
            "Nightly job: stalest rung, cheapest to operate",
            "Climb only when the correctness need is real"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Transaction Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Retry on `TransientTransactionError`",
            "Keep the body under 60 s",
            "Small snapshots — the cache is shared",
            "Ask first: could one document do it?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Measure, Do Not Guess",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.c.find(q).explain('executionStats')",
            "// nReturned, totalKeysExamined,",
            "// totalDocsExamined, executionTimeMillis"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Reading",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "keys ≈ docs ≈ returned",
              "index doing its job"
            ],
            [
              "keys >> returned",
              "scanning waste"
            ],
            [
              "docs examined = 0",
              "covered query, fastest"
            ],
            [
              "`COLLSCAN` stage",
              "no usable index"
            ],
            [
              "time up, count flat",
              "working set left RAM"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Slow Feed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.posts.find({user_id:u}).sort({t:-1})",
            "// before: COLLSCAN, 240k docs, 1.9 s",
            "db.posts.createIndex({user_id:1, t:-1})",
            "// after: 20 keys, 20 docs, 3 ms"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ESR again: equality `user_id`, then sort `t`",
            "`nReturned` never moved — examined work collapsed",
            "Same query text; only the plan changed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Read The Plan Top Down",
          "text": "`winningPlan` running `IXSCAN` then `FETCH` is healthy. A bare `COLLSCAN`, or a `SORT` stage with no index behind it, is the bill you are paying."
        }
      ]
    },
